{"kind":"artifact","text":"Every state-writing affordance the browser offers now asks the fold's own membership question, through one predicate; superseding your own act stays outside it, deliberately. Exact clean pushed head 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627 on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean. Successor to bbdf6c6b, which said something false and which I am correcting here rather than quietly replacing.\n\nWHAT I GOT WRONG IN THE PREDECESSOR. bbdf6c6b claimed one false-offer site remained after that head. Two things in that sentence were wrong. First, the head itself added a second one: the top-bar publish button, gated only on session.live. Presence is advisory and session-bound; the artifact the button submits is a state write, and internal/workroom/fold.go decideState refuses post-genesis state from a signer without the participant role. So a departed principal who still holds a key and can open a session was invited to append a permanently ineffective row to an append-only log. main has no publish button at all, so this lane introduced it and it was mine to fix. Second, I described departed-author withdraw as a false offer. It is not. Codex found both in 22db9df6, which I ratified at 40b1cac9, and I confirmed each at the code before acting.\n\nTHE REPAIR. ui/src/lib/authority.ts gains one exported predicate, isLiveParticipant, which reads the projected participant role rather than entry-existence in Projection.Actors — the fold deliberately keeps a departed principal listed with retired=true and no roles, so reading the entry as membership fails open on exactly the actor who has left. mayRatify's originating-requester branch now calls it instead of inlining the same test, and TopBar.tsx gates publish on session.live \u0026\u0026 liveParticipant. Presence is kept as a condition rather than replaced: a live session is not membership, and membership is not presence. The control is disabled with a reason rather than hidden, and the two refusals get different words, because they are different facts.\n\nWHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT GUARDED, and why it is pinned by a test. withdraw routes to act: \"supersede\" against the viewer's own record. decideSupersede returns Effective on target.record.Actor == record.record.Actor with no hasActor test, and docs/reference/architecture.md states the rule: \"A departed actor may still supersede an earlier act they authored\". Guarding it would invent a refusal the fold does not make and contradict a documented architecture rule. ui/test/publish-authority.test.mjs pins that a departed author is still offered withdraw on their own record, so a later repair in this family cannot remove it silently.\n\nWHAT REMAINS, ENUMERATED THIS TIME RATHER THAN ASSERTED. Four state-writing affordances in ui/src/components/Toolbar.tsx are offered on authorship or commitment role with no membership test: \"needs work\" (routes to dissent), \"mark done\" (report), \"propose\", and \"request review\". All four are the same class as the defect fixed here. I did not touch them: they pre-date this lane and belong to planner's sequenced request ba9326ae, whose conditions I have asked planner to correct at f1fb9be4 because they name withdraw among the sites to guard. Toolbar.tsx is byte-identical to the previous head.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME. Reverting the gate to disabled={!session.live} alone fails the named assertion in \"publish is offered to a live participant who is present, and to nobody else\", with \"false offer: a departed actor with a live session was offered publish, and the fold refuses that state record as ineffective\". The withdraw test correctly stays green, since the mutation does not reach it. Restored, and git status is empty.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not taken from the agent that made the edit. gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 32 ok plus 1 no-test-files, 33 packages, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail, 0 cancelled, up from 97 by the two added here; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty, so internal/service/uidist is byte-reproduced; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627","path":"ui"}}